  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1100 PM CST Wed Nov 4 2026\n\nThe aforementioned Canadian air mass will overtake the region this \nweekend with the surface high settling near the Mid Mississippi \nValley. We'll be very cool and stable this weekend as a result. \nRadiational cooling at night will promote our first widespread \nfrost and freeze of the season with lows well into the 30s. Some \nlocations in the Cumberland Valley could reach the upper 20s per \nlatest NBM data. Plan to protect any sensitive vegetation this \nweekend. Medium-range guidance depicts a fairly complex split \nflow pattern next week, but nothing in the way of systems aloft \nor meaningful moisture return across the Mid South. We'll should\nget a gradual air mass modification into mid-week that will \nsupport warming temperatures, though we'll remain rain-free \nthrough the forecast period.",
